  "summary": "Full assessment of all 198 English/Vietnamese passages in three parts and both titles, by two separate-context assessors who read every pair and checked consistency across the three drafting parts. The Nellie frame, Brussels, the Outer and Central Stations, the river journey, the attack, the Russian, Kurtz’s death, Marlow’s illness and the lie to the Intended are complete, with Conrad’s density and the period vocabulary rendered faithfully. The assessors scored the halves 8.80 and 8.925 with no major findings; their minor findings were revised. Fidelity, voice, imagery and mechanics are 9.0, naturalness 8.5. Unrounded weighted score 8.925 meets the unchanged 8.6 threshold. No unresolved major or critical issue remains.",
  "title_review": {
    "source_title": "Heart of Darkness",
    "target_title": "Trái tim của bóng tối",
    "rationale": "Trái tim của bóng tối echoes the in-text phrase ‘vào trái tim của bóng tối’ as Conrad’s title echoes his text; Tâm bóng tối loses the bodily heart."
  }
